  "note": "IFRS and DART taxonomy concepts that appear on a Korean income statement, and what each one is. Data, not code, so an accountant can review and diff it. A concept is a *language-independent identifier*: mapping on it removes caption matching entirely, which is where every ingest defect so far has come from. 'nature' gives the sign — an XBRL filing reports a deduction as a positive figure and leaves the sign to the taxonomy. 'subtotal' names a figure the filing itself computed; those are reconciliation targets, never inputs (spec §17). 'order' is the order a Korean income statement prints these in.",
